A||||1||theogre||Stoping a Temp Guage from pegging
Z||000000||theogre||05-18-99||02:26 PM||||Well, I finally got time to check out the temp gauge wiring and redo it so that it stops pegging when starting the car.<p>Here's what I found doing this project.<p>1. You can do this with no harness cutting at all. The terminals to fit the ignition switch are available at many auto parts shops, or can be scavenged from any of several other connectors on a junk car. (I had extras from the installation of the power trunk latch option. The PT, and Rdefog, switches use them.)<br>2. Most methods tell you to pull the dash. You don't need to do that. Take out the 2 bolts, and loosen the 2 nuts that hold up the steering column. Then you can get to the ignition switch. This way you only have to remove the back of the dash to access the connector on the passenger side. (Even with the dash removed getting the ignition connector is ver difficult without dropping the column.)<br>3. You can use a crimp on wiretap to connect the new wire to the dark green wire in the dash. You don’t need to unplug the dash at all. (These are blue, and have a little metal tab you crush into the 2 wires. A small flap then snaps over to insulate the connection.) There is only 1 dark green wire in the passenger side connector on the back of the dash.<br>4. If you do cut the light green wire from the ignition switch. You can simply extend it using crimp on connectors to reach the Dark green wire. If you are cutting the light green wire you don’t need to remove anything but the under dash trim, and dash back.<br>5. Working time for this project should be under 1 hour. (I did mine in a local park during lunch.)<br>6. The best version of the instructions for this repair that I’ve found is here:  <A HREF="http://www.tir.com/~jaski/tempgauge/tempgauge.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tir.com/~jaski/tempgauge/tempgauge.htm</A>  It’s got good pictures of the connectors.<br>
Z||000001||Pretender||05-19-99||12:02 AM||||mine also peggs when i start the car, but a good wack is all it takes, :o)., but i do plan on fixing it soon!, nothing more embarrasing then when your on a date and you have to hit the dash cluster everytime you start the car...thanks for the instructions ogre!..
